# PowerShell scripts are byte-for-byte.
#
# work-setup.ps1 is saved with a UTF-8 BOM on purpose: Windows PowerShell 5.1
# reads a BOM-less script as the ANSI codepage, which silently corrupts every
# non-ASCII character the script writes out. Line-ending or encoding rewriting
# by Git would undo that, so these files are marked binary-safe.
*.ps1 -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF, whatever the platform they are checked out on.
*.sh text eol=lf
